+## `dlt dashboard`
+
+Launches the pipeline dashboard app.
+
+**Usage**
+```sh
+dlt dashboard [-h] [--pipelines-dir PIPELINES_DIR] [--edit]
+```
+
+**Description**
+
+The `dlt dashboard` command starts the dlt pipeline dashboard. You can use the dashboard to inspect the pipeline state, schemas, and data in the destination. It should be executed from the same folder from which you ran the pipeline script to access destination credentials.
+
+Requires `marimo` to be installed in the current environment: `pip install marimo`.
+
+<details>
+
+<summary>Show Arguments and Options</summary>
+
+Inherits arguments from [`dlt`](#dlt).
+
+**Options**
+* `-h, --help` - Show this help message and exit
+* `--pipelines-dir PIPELINES_DIR` - Pipelines working directory
+* `--edit` - Eject Dashboard and start editable version
+
+</details>
